===Etymology===
{{root|ru|ine-pro|*gʰedʰ-}}
From {{inh|ru|orv|годъ||time, period, year, age}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*godъ||suitable time}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-bsl-pro|*gadás}}, from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*gʰodʰo-}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*gʰedʰ-||to unite, be associated, be suitable}}.

Cognates include
{{cog|uk|годі||enough}},
{{cog|bg|годе||[[ever]]}} (as in {{l|bg|кой-годе}} = whoever),
{{cog|cs|hod}},
{{cog|pl|gody||yearly feast}},
{{cog|hsb|hody||Christmas}},
{{cog|dsb|gódy||Christmas}},
{{cog|lv|gadigs}}.

Germanic cognates include
{{cog|de|Gatte||husband}}, {{m|de|gätlich||convenient}},
{{cog|nl|gegade}}, {{m|nl|gade}}, {{m|nl|gading}},
{{cog|nl|gader}}, {{m|nl|goed}},
{{cog|de|gut}}, as well as {{cog|en|gather}}, {{m|en|together}} and {{m|en|good}}.

